  "summary": "Minimalist REST API contract for task management, defining standard CRUD operations and a simplified Task resource model using a strict, lightweight JSON specification.",
  "approach": "Design a stateless RESTful API utilizing standard HTTP methods and resource-oriented URIs. The API contract is defined as a simplified JSON document detailing paths, methods, and payload schemas for the Task resource, omitting OpenAPI boilerplate to maintain strict minimalism.",
  "tradeoffs": [
    "Using a custom simplified JSON contract instead of OpenAPI reduces standard tooling compatibility but significantly decreases verbosity and complexity.",
    "Omitting pagination and filtering parameters in the GET /tasks endpoint simplifies the design but may require future refactoring for large datasets."
  ],
  "evidence": [
    "REST architectural style constraints advocate for resource-based URIs and standard HTTP methods to ensure uniform interface.",
    "Minimalist API design principles prioritize core CRUD operations to accelerate client integration and reduce cognitive load."
  ],
